  "userDescription": "## Authority\n\nAuthoritative guest-services record for hotel guests and their service journeys.\n\n## Use this source for\n\n- Guest identity, reservations, stays, room assignments, and dining reservations.\n- Folios, transactions, payments, adjustments, disputes, and special requests.\n- Confirmation, idempotency, audit, and reconciliation workflow records.\n\n## Boundary\n\nOfficial property, room, inventory, rate, outlet, maintenance, and work-order facts belong to HotelOperations.",
  "dataSourceInstructions": "Use HotelGuestServices for authoritative guest-facing reads and curated guest-service facts; use HotelOperations to resolve official property names. Search exact identifiers across all dates unless a date filter is requested. Use 2026-09-01 as the fixed temporal boundary: past reservations require check_in < DATE '2026-09-01', future or upcoming reservations require check_in > DATE '2026-09-01' and normally status IN ('future','arriving'), and records dated 2026-09-01 are excluded from both groups. Data dictionary: `reservations` stores booking records. Fields: `reservation_id` is the confirmation key; `property_id` joins the hotel; `check_in` is arrival date; `status` is lifecycle state; `channel` is booking origin. `folios` stores stay account balances. Fields: `folio_id` is the account key; `property_id` joins the hotel; `balance` is the unpaid amount. `billing_disputes` stores contested fees. Fields: `billing_dispute_id` is the case key; `folio_id` joins its account; `status` is case state; `amount` is the disputed monetary value. `agg_property_kpis_daily` stores daily property facts. Fields: `service_date` is business date; `occupied_rooms` and `sellable_rooms` are inventory counts; `room_revenue` is revenue in property currency. `action_sagas` stores cross-source workflow state. Fields: `saga_id` is the workflow key; `state` is progress; `pending_reconciliation` flags incomplete reconciliation.",
